  "conclusion": "Our Sec 4.2 exact bias law reproduces the CGK mechanism: per-qubit depolarizing drives Tr(sigma^2) -> 2^-n under both hypotheses, so the testing gap Delta closes exponentially (base (1+3(1-lambda)^2)/4). The implied SWAP-test shot count 1/Delta^2 grows exponentially with asymptotic base (4/(1+3(1-lambda)^2))^2, which is >= CGK's lower-bound base b(lambda)=4/(1+3(1-lambda)^4) for all lambda (equality at lambda=0), via the identity 4(1+3x^2)-(1+3x)^2 = 3(1-x)^2 >= 0 with x=(1-lambda)^2. The SWAP-test cost 1/Delta^2 lies at or above the CGK universal lower bound at every (n,lambda) tested, as required."
